Falsifies `inter_process_communication::notification::verification::a_signal_loses_no_bit`.

The defect: the bound delivery hands over only the new bits and clears the word, dropping
whatever accumulated while the bound thread was elsewhere. It reads naturally, because the signal
"is" the bits it carried.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(delivered | n.word, before | bits)` whenever the word was non-zero
before a bound-receiving signal.

